  "excerpt": "Key Takeaways Most wrongful death settlements in Colorado remain non-taxable when tied to physical injury compensation. Certain portions, like punitive damages or interest, may still create tax obligations under IRS rules. Emotional distress damages qualify as taxable only when unrelated to physical injury or illness. Settlement structure and allocation can influence whether any tax applies […]",
